[[6,1,524288,"<h2>Introduction</h2><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001024.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1 - C514R M.T. gearbox</li><li>2 - Front differential</li><li>3 - Drive</li><li>4 - Propeller shaft (in two pieces)</li><li>5 - Viscous coupling</li><li>6 - Rear differential</li></ul></figure><h3>Drive torque and grip</h3><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001025.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>Figure A</li></ul></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001026.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>Figure B</li></ul></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001027.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>Figure C</li></ul></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001028.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>Figure D</li></ul></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169000949.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>Figure E</li></ul></figure><h2>Four wheel drive</h2><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001029.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>Figure F</li></ul></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001030.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><h3>Permanent four wheel drive</h3><ul><li>Vehicles with the drive constantly distributed between the axles: a centre differential distributes the drive to the front and to the rear constantly (for example, the Lancia Delta 4x4 where the epicyclic centre differential distributes 56% of the drive to the front and 44% to the rear)</li><li>Vehicles with the drive distributed in a variable manner: these vehicles are usually equipped with a viscous coupling which modulates the percentage of drive shared between the front and the rear (e.g. the Fiat Panda 4x4).</li></ul><h3>Four wheel drive that can be switched on</h3><h2>Transmission of power</h2><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001031.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1 - Layshaft</li><li>2 - Ring gear</li><li>3 - Front differential</li><li>4 - Drive</li><li>5 - Idler unit</li><li>6 - Propeller shaft (in two pieces)</li><li>7 - Viscous coupling</li><li>8 - Rear differential</li><li>9 - Driveshafts</li></ul></figure><h2>Drive and idler unit</h2><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>If the differential ring gear is being replaced, only use the specific replacement part for the 4x4 version.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001032.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1 - Pinion</li><li>2 - Ring gear</li><li>3 - Conical gears</li><li>4 - Flange</li></ul></figure><h2>Propeller shaft</h2><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001033.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1 - Front section</li><li>2 - Universal joints</li><li>3 - Bearing</li><li>4 - Flexible mounting</li><li>5 - Bracket</li><li>6 - Rear section</li></ul></figure><h2>Viscous coupling</h2><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001034.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1 - Viscous coupling</li><li>2 - Rear differential</li></ul></figure><h3>Operation</h3><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/768.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>Towing the vehicle with only the front wheels raised off the ground unable to rotate may lead to damage of the coupling and/or wear of the tyres.</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001035.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>Figure G</li><li>ni : viscous coupling input revs</li><li>no : viscous coupling output revs</li></ul></figure><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001036.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1 - Viscous coupling outer casing (flanged to the propeller shaft)</li><li>2 - Splined shaft (for connecting the rear differential pinion)</li><li>3 - Set of metal discs</li></ul></figure><h2>Rear differential</h2><aside class=\"note\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/767.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><p>The pinion (1) receives the drive torque transmitted from the propeller shaft from the viscous coupling (8).</p></aside><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/169001037.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><ul class=\"legend\"><li>1 - Pinion</li><li>2 - Ring gear</li><li>3 - Differential unit</li><li>4 - Pin</li><li>5 - Satellite gears</li><li>6 - Planet gears</li><li>7 - Couplings</li><li>8 - Viscous coupling</li></ul></figure><h2>Deceleration anti-slip system (MSR)</h2>"]]